Set GitHub Secrets (in repo Settings → Secrets)

DOCKER_USERNAME
DOCKER_PASSWORD (Docker Hub token)
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
AWS_REGION (e.g., us-east-1)
EKS_CLUSTER_NAME
Update k8s manifests with actual values:

Replace docker-registry.example.com/ → your Docker Hub username
Replace example.com → your actual domain
Update secret values in secrets.yaml (S3 bucket, DB URL, JWT secret, etc.)
Setup AWS infrastructure (one-time):

RDS PostgreSQL database
ElastiCache Redis cluster
S3 bucket
IAM role
Push to main → workflow auto-triggers, builds all images, deploys to EKS